    fix(fframes-3d): classify the fabric effects the port does not draw
    
    Two effects a garment scene can ask for were selectable without failing:
    
    - garmentCut. The source's colour pass discards outside the panel cut and
      repeats exactly those cuts in a depth material (cloth/fabric_glsl.js:479-495,
      fabricDepth: "hero.js shells are supersets of the garment cut ... this depth
      material runs hero.js's own cuts"), so an uncut shell also casts a shadow it
      should not. The cut depends on the garment construction (region, along, the
      per-kind block), which this path does not carry: the path draws the whole
      shell.
    - wear.zones. The source's zone-driven abrasion (knees, seat, elbows, the lap,
      zoneK in FAB_WEAR) is not carried; the wear here is crest and seam driven.
    
    Both are now in fabric's unsupported list with the citations above, so
    require() fails and require_classified() accepts the names as considered. A
    test pins that they are refused and classified, and that garmentCut is not
    claimed as a feature.
    
    (Found while completing the fabric classification: wear.zones had been dropped
    from the list in an earlier edit.)

